```bash
python -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install fastapi "pydantic>=2,<3" pytest httpx coverage ruff
export PYTHONPATH=runs/kit/REQ-002/src
mkdir -p runs/kit/REQ-002/reports
python -m pytest runs/kit/REQ-002/test/backend/auth/test_req_behavior.py -q --maxfail=1 --junitxml=runs/kit/REQ-002/reports/pytest-junit.xml
python -m coverage run -m pytest runs/kit/REQ-002/test/backend/auth/test_req_behavior.py -q
python -m coverage xml -o runs/kit/REQ-002/reports/coverage.xml
python -m ruff check runs/kit/REQ-002/src runs/kit/REQ-002/test > runs/kit/REQ-002/reports/ruff.txt
```

## Assumptions

- Upstream infrastructure has already authenticated the caller and forwards claim payloads to the backend.
- This slice enforces normalized actor context and RBAC from forwarded claims; it does not replace upstream token validation.
- The protected write endpoint uses in-memory sinks to make the authorization and propagation seam locally testable. During promotion, those sinks should be wired to canonical business-write and audit implementations.
- Claim-to-permission mapping is attribute-based through groups, roles, permission claims, and scopes. There are no profile-specific authorization branches or username allowlists.

## Gaps

- No direct import of an existing shared actor contract was possible from the isolated staging payload; the emitted `ActorContext.audit_actor()` shape is designed to be bound cleanly into shared downstream contracts at promotion time.
- Only the auth-focused endpoints required to prove REQ-002 are emitted here. Broader application router integration remains outside this REQ.

